# Integrity: scripts/verify.py SHA-256s the corpus files byte-for-byte and compares
# them to data/checksums.json. Git's autocrlf on Windows rewrites LF -> CRLF at
# checkout, which changes those bytes and makes the gatekeeper report
#     "eval sets unmodified: FAIL ... Editing the eval set after seeing results
#      invalidates the comparison"
# on a clone nobody has touched. Mark the checksummed data as binary so no platform
# rewrites it. The checksums in data/checksums.json are the LF ones.
data/*.jsonl -text
